WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.680
For years, fans have been enjoying Pawn Stars,
the reality show about the Harrison family

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.539
and their famed Gold and Silver Pawn Shop
in Las Vegas.

00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:12.300
But this isn't even the family's first taste
of TV stardom, as they were previously featured

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.900
on both Comedy Central and PBS.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.740
And before that, the cast members each had
long and interesting lives and careers outside

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.080
of television.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.080
Surprised?

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.170
Here's a look at the Pawn Stars before all
the fame.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.909
The Old Man

00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:30.909
Richard Benjamin Harrison, better known as
"the Old Man," was born on March 4, 1941 in

00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:36.610
Danville, Virginia, to what his son Rick described
in his 2011 memoir License to Pawn as "dirt

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.270
poor white trash, left to survive on their
wits."

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.370
He helped the family make ends meet by driving
a school bus at the age of 14...which had

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:49.780
to be pretty surreal for the other kids on
the bus.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.760
In 1960, Richard's life changed drastically.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.561
Just before his marriage to a girl named Joanne
Rhue, who he met at a barn dance, Richard

00:00:56.561 --> 00:00:58.350
was arrested for stealing a car.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.250
Instead of serving jail time, he chose to
join the Navy.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.659
He served for 20 years, eventually moving
the family to the naval hub of San Diego,

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:07.690
where he and his wife took up real estate.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.720
But when the housing market collapsed in the
early '80s, he decided to switch careers,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.200
moving his family to Las Vegas to focus on
buying and selling gold.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.550
And the rest, as they say, is history.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.550
Rick Harrison

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:24.090
The charismatic face of Pawn Stars, Rick Harrison's
early life was a struggle.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.351
Diagnosed with epilepsy at age eight, Rick
was confined to his bed for treatment, and

00:01:28.351 --> 00:01:33.590
found his escape in reading — and eventually
in drugs, which began with a joint in fourth

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:34.590
grade.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.440
By the time the family moved to Las Vegas,
Rick had become a slick wheeler dealer, selling

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.510
fake Gucci bags to pay the bills.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.909
He quit that gig to help The Old Man open
a pawn shop, but there was one problem: local

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.280
laws banned pawn shops inside the city limits
until the city's population hit a quarter

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.479
of a million people.

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:55.520
That delayed the dream, but didn't end it,
and in 1988 the Gold and Silver Pawn Shop

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.689
opened its doors with an initial investment
of just $10,000.

00:01:58.689 --> 00:02:00.970
Big Hoss

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:07.070
Born to Rick on April 27, 1983, when Rick
was just 18, Corey's childhood took place

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.190
almost entirely inside the Gold and Silver
Pawn Shop.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.510
He started working at the shop at the age
of nine, eventually turning that entry level

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:18.240
position at the store polishing jewelry into
a managerial position with a five percent

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.020
cut and the promise of taking over the family
business once Rick and The Old Man retire.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:29.260
In 2011, The Big Hoss got a lot smaller, shedding
close to 200 pounds thanks to gastric lap-band

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.630
surgery and dietary changes designed to help
stave off the possibility of diabetes.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.790
Good job, Big Hoss!

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.810
Chumlee

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.530
The goofy "honorary member" of the family
who always seems a step away from getting

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.640
fired, Austin "Chumlee" Russell was born on
September 8, 1982.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.599
His nickname of "Chumlee" came from the cartoon
Tennessee Tuxedo, "Chumley" being the walrus

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:52.750
sidekick of the titular penguin lead.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:56.170
"Now Chumley, will you please toss up the
Sports section?"

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.110
"I'll bring it myself!"

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.160
A childhood friend of Corey's, Chumlee joined
the staff of the Gold and Silver when he was

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.240
21, and has been a constant presence at the
shop ever since, including at the Harrison's

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.240
Christmas dinner.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.841
The Harrisons love to make light of their
friend and his semi-frequent lapses in judgment.

00:03:11.841 --> 00:03:14.440
"Why don't they just make Cuban cigars in
America?"

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.570
"Chumlee that's probably one of the dumbest
things you ever said."

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.900
Despite that — or perhaps because of it
— he's widely considered the most popular

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.360
member of the group, with the shop's own profile
page claiming girls get nervous around him

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.330
"like perhaps One Direction or the Biebs has
just walked into the room."

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.140
Take that with a grain of salt, of course.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.160
But there's no denying that Chum is an aid
to the Harrisons, especially with his knowledge

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.989
of games, pinball machines, and sneakers.

00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:40.830
By God, that man loves his sneakers.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.300
"This is a lot of my collection.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.700
But it's not really it, this isn't everything."

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.780
Thanks for watching!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.060
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.160
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love, too!

